From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] msdasql: foreign key, index and provider type schema rowsets

IDBSchemaRowset gives DBSCHEMA_FOREIGN_KEYS (SQLForeignKeys; update/delete rules as the OLE DB rule names, deferrability mapped), DBSCHEMA_INDEXES (SQLStatistics, its table statistics rows left out; uniqueness, clustering, type, collation mapped) and DBSCHEMA_PROVIDER_TYPES (SQLGetTypeInfo; types, searchability, long types mapped). A catalog row's ODBC columns are now read once each and shared (several OLE DB columns come from one, and SQLGetData gives a column only once). They were E_INVALIDARG.
---
--- a/dlls/msdasql/session.c
+++ b/dlls/msdasql/session.c
@@ -843,7 +843,9 @@
 
 /* Stained Glass OS: the columns of an OLE DB schema rowset and the ODBC catalog
  * function's columns they come from */
-enum schema_conv { SC_COPY, SC_NULL, SC_NULLABLE_BOOL, SC_SQLTYPE_TO_DBTYPE, SC_IF_CHAR, SC_IF_NUMERIC, SC_HAS_VALUE };
+enum schema_conv { SC_COPY, SC_NULL, SC_NULLABLE_BOOL, SC_SQLTYPE_TO_DBTYPE, SC_IF_CHAR, SC_IF_NUMERIC, SC_HAS_VALUE,
+                   /* (wine-sg 8224) */ SC_RULE, SC_DEFERRABILITY, SC_BOOL, SC_NOT_BOOL, SC_EQ1_BOOL, SC_INDEX_TYPE,
+                   SC_COLLATION, SC_SEARCHABLE, SC_IS_LONG };
 
